.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Component\\n\\nConfig\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\n\\nAs per the spec:\\n\\n> Setting the [OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk-environment-variables.md#declarative-configuration) environment variable (for languages that support it) provides users a convenient way to initialize OpenTelemetry components without needing to learn language-specific configuration details or use a large number of environment variables. The pattern for accessing the configured components and installing into instrumentation will vary by language. For example, the usage in Java might resemble:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk.md#via-otel_experimental_config_file\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nOpen to suggestions of how this should be implemented to align w/ the rest of the Go SDK implementation\\n\\n### Alternatives\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Prior Art\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Context\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (2)\\n\\n**codeboten** — 2025-10-23T17:18:25Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack descript compon config problem statement a per the spec set the otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk environ variabl md declar configur environ variabl for languag that support it provid user a conveni way to initi opentelemetri compon without need to learn languag specif configur detail or use a larg number of environ variabl the pattern for access the configur compon and instal into instrument will vari by languag for exampl the usag in java might resembl http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk md via otel _ experiment _ config _ file propos solut open to suggest of how this should be implement to align w the rest of the go sdk implement altern _ no respons _ prior art _ no respons _ addit context _ no respons _ sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack discuss 2 codeboten 2025 10 23t17 18 25z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"id\": \"d162a2a65d87b225\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3176531451800102, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11363636454287179, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7936923, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request akats7 2025 11 10t04 27 26z yile j i think we re good to resolv the conflict and close this out 