similarity\": 0.3551786517073696, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1845078767248138, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75341046, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Component\\n\\nConfig\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\n\\nAs per the spec:\\n\\n> Setting the [OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk-environment-variables.md#declarative-configuration) environment variable (for languages that support it) provides users a convenient way to initialize OpenTelemetry components without needing to learn language-specific configuration details or use a large number of environment variables. The pattern for accessing the configured components and installing into instrumentation will vary by language. For example, the usage in Java might resemble:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk.md#via-otel_experimental_config_file\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nOpen to suggestions of how this should be implemented to align w/ the rest of the Go SDK implementation\\n\\n### Alternatives\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Prior Art\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Context\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (2)\\n\\n**codeboten** — 2025-10-23T17:18:25Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack descript compon config problem statement a per the spec set the otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk environ variabl md declar configur environ variabl for languag that support it provid user a conveni way to initi opentelemetri compon without need to learn languag specif configur detail or use a larg number of environ variabl the pattern for access the configur compon and instal into instrument will vari by languag for exampl the usag in java might resembl http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk md via otel _ experiment _ config _ file propos solut open to suggest of how this should be implement to align w the rest of the go sdk implement altern _ no respons _ prior art _ no respons _ addit context _ no respons _ sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack discuss 2 codeboten 2025 10 23t17 18 25z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"id\": \"d162a2a65d87b225\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32475414483337495, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14794050690482138, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7373193, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3029512308903263, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12540802984332328, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7172187, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    - Advantages:\\n\\n      - Avoids SDK import cycles and keeps experimental behavior isolated.\\n\\n      - Lets users opt in; easier to iterate and gather feedback before considering SDK-level integration.\\n\\n- Global vs. explicit provider setup:\\n\\n  - The otel global package has its own subtleties; supporting both code paths may be necessary.\\n\\n  - Global setup increases risk of cycles/complexity; explicit function in contrib is cleaner initially.\\n\\n- Tentative direction:\\n\\n  - Do not add SDK-level support in the short term.\\n\\n  - Prototype in contrib (otelconf); gather user feedback.\\n\\n  - Revisit SDK inclusion later if demand and design stabilize.\\n\\n### Auto-instrumentation considerations\\n\\n- Go auto-instrumentation would likely benefit from config-file-driven setup, but it can build on the contrib implementation once it exists.\\n\\n### SDK experimental features README gap\\n\\n- There is an “observability” feature in an internal X package that is not documented in the README; should be updated.\\n\\n### Metrics pipeline and exponential histogram status\\n\\n- David:\\n\\n  - Working on exponential histogram; close to resolving one remaining issue (race condition).\\n\\n  - Performance is faster but currently ~150 ns vs. a ~120 ns goal; investigating sources of overhead (likely computation).\\n\\n- Tyler:\\n\\n  - Still owes reviews on metrics pipeline optimization PRs.\\n\\n  - Discussed exemplar/histogram locking changes; some PRs shift lock scope; others use a hot/cold structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- Alex: Draft a proposal/PR in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf to:\\n\\n  - Load and apply OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE via an explicit function that returns configured SDK providers.\\n\\n  - Optionally provide an init-based variant guarded by the env var for experimentation (clearly documented).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"advantag avoid sdk import cycl and keep experiment behavior isol let user opt in easier to iter and gather feedback befor consid sdk level integr global v explicit provid setup the otel global packag ha it own subtleti support both code path may be necessari global setup increas risk of cycl complex explicit function in contrib is cleaner initi tentat direct do not add sdk level support in the short term prototyp in contrib otelconf gather user feedback revisit sdk inclus later if demand and design stabil auto instrument consider go auto instrument would like benefit from config file driven setup but it can build on the contrib implement onc it exist sdk experiment featur readm gap there is an observ featur in an intern x packag that is not document in the readm should be updat metric pipelin and exponenti histogram status david work on exponenti histogram close to resolv one remain issu race condit perform is faster but current 150 n v a 120 n goal investig sourc of overhead like comput tyler still owe review on metric pipelin optim pr discuss exemplar histogram lock chang some pr shift lock scope other use a hot cold structur sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol action item alex draft a propos pr in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf to load and appli otel _ experiment _ config _ file via an explicit function that return configur sdk provid option provid an init base variant guard by the env var for experiment clear document\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1109a6ade747ca21\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27835301640239835, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1026479520034262, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6883315, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Two non-observability items noted:\\n\\n  - Sync map / atomics for fixed bucket histograms.\\n\\n  - Exemplar reservoir changes.\\n\\n- Safe to slip to next release; include if ready.\\n\\n### 4. Stabilizing new attribute value types\\n\\n- Discussion about stabilizing new spec attribute types (byte arrays, “any” type).\\n\\n- Prototype implementation exists and needs review.\\n\\n- Considered tricky; careful review needed around limits and types.\\n\\n### 5. Processor `Enabled` method\\n\\n- Proposal from Robert to move `Enabled` from filter processor to main processor interface.\\n\\n- Spec now stabilized and allows this.\\n\\n- Pros: consistent API, less ad-hoc type assertion/boilerplate in docs.\\n\\n- Con: processors that are “always enabled” need a trivial `Enabled() bool { return true }`.\\n\\n- General agreement; will revisit for final confirmation.\\n\\n### 6. OTLP `insecure` support (logs, env vars, spec)\\n\\n- PR adds `insecure` (env var) support for OTLP **logs**, matching traces/metrics.\\n\\n- HTTP OTLP config historically messy; env vars common in practice.\\n\\n- Spec unclear due to moratorium on env vars.\\n\\n- Direction: add logs support in Go; push for spec clarity later.\\n\\n### 7. Collector protobuf changes & PDataGen\\n\\n- Collector removed dependency on Go protobuf types; now uses `pdataGen`.\\n\\n- Large internal rewrite; significant line count reduction.\\n\\n- Benchmarks improved (fewer allocations).\\n\\n- Some cross-language quirks surfaced but manageable.\\n\\n- Go SIG interested in exploring similar approaches; needs more benchmarking.\\n\\n### 8. KubeCon & talks\\n\\n- First SIG meeting since KubeCon.\\n\\n- Members encouraged to share notable talks and videos once available.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Merge OTelConf RC support PR as-is (pending normal review).\\n\\n- Track experimental API structure review (e.g., `x` submodule) under the `1.40.0` milestone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"two non observ item note sync map atom for fix bucket histogram exemplar reservoir chang safe to slip to next releas includ if readi 4 stabil new attribut valu type discuss about stabil new spec attribut type byte array ani type prototyp implement exist and need review consid tricki care review need around limit and type 5 processor enabl method propos from robert to move enabl from filter processor to main processor interfac spec now stabil and allow this pro consist api less ad hoc type assert boilerpl in doc con processor that are alway enabl need a trivial enabl bool return true general agreement will revisit for final confirm 6 otlp insecur support log env var spec pr add insecur env var support for otlp log match trace metric http otlp config histor messi env var common in practic spec unclear due to moratorium on env var direct add log support in go push for spec clariti later 7 collector protobuf chang pdatagen collector remov depend on go protobuf type now us pdatagen larg intern rewrit signific line count reduct benchmark improv fewer alloc some cross languag quirk surfac but manag go sig interest in explor similar approach need more benchmark 8 kubecon talk first sig meet sinc kubecon member encourag to share notabl talk and video onc avail sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 decis merg otelconf rc support pr ais pend normal review track experiment api structur review e g x submodul under the 140 0 mileston\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"2174523acdce943d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2738549591584344, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09126791308347766, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6998914, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp`. (#7512)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for manual reader in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7524)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for periodic reader in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7571)\\n\\n- Support `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_INSECURE` and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE` environmental variables in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp`. (#7608)\\n\\n- Add `Enabled` method to the `Processor` interface in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`. All `Processor` implementations now include an `Enabled` method. (#7639)\\n\\n- The `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.38.0` package. The package contains semantic conventions from the `v1.38.0` version of the OpenTelemetry Semantic Conventions. See the [migration documentation](./semconv/v1.38.0/MIGRATION.md) for information on how to upgrade from `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0.`(#7648)\\n\\n### Changed\\n\\n- `Distinct` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` is no longer guaranteed to uniquely identify an attribute set. Collisions between `Distinct` values for different Sets are possible with extremely high cardinality (billions of series per instrument), but are highly unlikely. (#7175)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `TracerOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/meter` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `MeterOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- `WithInstrumentationAttributes` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` synchronously de-duplicates the passed attributes instead of delegating it to the returned `LoggerOption`. (#7266)\\n\\n- Rename the `OTEL_GO_X_SELF_OBSERVABILITY` environment variable to `OTEL_GO_X_OBSERVABILITY` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/stdout/stdouttrace`. (#7302)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploghttp 7512 add experiment observ metric for manual reader in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7524 add experiment observ metric for period reader in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7571 support otel _ export _ otlp _ log _ insecur and otel _ export _ otlp _ insecur environment variabl in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploghttp 7608 add enabl method to the processor interfac in go opentelemetri io otel sdk log all processor implement now includ an enabl method 7639 the go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 38 0 packag the packag contain semant convent from the v1 38 0 version of the opentelemetri semant convent see the migrat document semconv v1 38 0 migrat md for inform on how to upgrad from go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 37 0 7648 chang distinct in go opentelemetri io otel attribut is no longer guarante to uniqu identifi an attribut set collis between distinct valu for differ set are possibl with extrem high cardin billion of seri per instrument but are high unlik 7175 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel trace synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return traceropt 7266 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel meter synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return meteropt 7266 withinstrumentationattribut in go opentelemetri io otel log synchron de duplic the pass attribut instead of deleg it to the return loggeropt 7266 renam the otel _ go _ x _ self _ observ environ variabl to otel _ go _ x _ observ in go opentelemetri io otel sdk trace go opentelemetri io otel sdk log and go opentelemetri io otel export stdout stdouttrac 7302\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"6a08b40f9cb6a8a6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26292890612562714, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0682802344651816, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71710914, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- Robert:\\n\\n  - Work with GC to set up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications and ensure appropriate access for Go SIG maintainers.\\n\\n  - Consider manual recreation of older OSS-Fuzz issues if needed; revisit auto GitHub issue filing after triage process matures.\\n\\n  - Take ownership of otelhttp issue [#7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254); draft a document clarifying error marking approach and semconv alignment.\\n\\n  - Enable GitHub signature releases for OTel Go; update releasing docs; ensure artifacts are uploaded at release time and signatures published. Reference: [sig-security #164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164).\\n\\n- Damien:\\n\\n  - Open an issue to kick off an audit of the otelhttp API for stabilization and coordinate reviews.\\n\\n- David (dashpole):\\n\\n  - Monitor semconv RPC stabilization efforts; once stable, drive otelgrpc module stabilization.\\n\\n  - Sync with Josh regarding gRPC team engagement; explore KubeCon conversations if feasible.\\n\\n- Mike:\\n\\n  - Iterate on the otel Explorer Go docs schema:\\n\\n    - Align with OTEL semantic conventions.\\n\\n    - Ensure Weaver compatibility.\\n\\n    - Provide a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation.\\n\\n    - Consider linking instrumentations to existing semconv references.\\n\\n- Tyler:\\n\\n  - Assign relevant GitHub tasks/issues from this meeting.\\n\\n  - Confirm KubeCon schedule and cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; share booth details with the community.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum action item robert work with gc to set up a maintain mail list for os fuzz notif and ensur appropri access for go sig maintain consid manual recreat of older os fuzz issu if need revisit auto github issu file after triag process matur take ownership of otelhttp issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 draft a document clarifi error mark approach and semconv align enabl github signatur releas for otel go updat releas doc ensur artifact are upload at releas time and signatur publish refer sig secur 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 damien open an issu to kick off an audit of the otelhttp api for stabil and coordin review david dashpol monitor semconv rpc stabil effort onc stabl drive otelgrpc modul stabil sync with josh regard grpc team engag explor kubecon convers if feasibl mike iter on the otel explor go doc schema align with otel semant convent ensur weaver compat provid a json schema or cue for valid consid link instrument to exist semconv refer tyler assign relev github task issu from this meet confirm kubecon schedul and cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week share booth detail with the communiti\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"21d887bde8f8d5d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24824293412562712, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0682802344651816, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6681559, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-03]\\n\\n# Issue: Recommend immutable releases (open-telemetry/sig-security#164)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164  \\n\\n**Author**: trask  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-08-27T13:31:30Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-28T22:16:50Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nhttps://github.blog/changelog/2025-08-26-releases-now-support-immutability-in-public-preview/\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-03]\\n\\n# Issue: Recommend immutable releases (open-telemetry/sig-security#164)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164  \\n\\n**Author**: trask  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-08-27T13:31:30Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-28T22:16:50Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (9)\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-09-16T12:52:39Z\\n\\nI tested it on my side-project\\n\\nCheck: https://github.com/goyek/goyek/releases/tag/v2.3.0 and notice the \\\"Immutable\\\" text and icon as well as \\n\\n\\\"Release attestation (json)\\\" in the release assets .\\n\\nTesting:\\n\\n```\\n\\n$ gh release verify v2.3.0 --repo goyek/goyek\\n\\nResolved tag v2.3.0 to sha1:580d400496e680ca42e42e5101f591dc1e6a747c\\n\\nLoaded attestation from GitHub API\\n\\n✓ Release v2.3.0 verified!\\n\\n```\\n\\n> [!CAUTION]\\n\\n> It is not possible to add/edit/remove release assets (artifacts) after the release is published. \\n\\n> This is great, but maybe some repositories add the assets after the release is already published. The release process must be checked for the repositories before enabling the feature.\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\n> This command cannot be used to verify the source code zip file or tarball for a release, since these assets are only created when a download is requested.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston descript http github blog changelog 2025 08 26 releas now support immut in public preview sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston discuss 9 pellar 2025 09 16t12 52 39z i test it on my side project check http github com goyek goyek releas tag v2 3 0 and notic the immut text and icon a well a releas attest json in the releas asset test gh releas verifi v2 3 0 repo goyek goyek resolv tag v2 3 0 to sha1 580d400496e680ca42e42e5101f591dc1e6a747c load attest from github api releas v2 3 0 verifi caution it is not possibl to add edit remov releas asset artifact after the releas is publish this is great but mayb some repositori add the asset after the releas is alreadi publish the releas process must be check for the repositori befor enabl the featur import this command can not be use to verifi the sourc code zip file or tarbal for a releas sinc these asset are onli creat when a download is request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"850c33a1966bb99c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24497573912562712, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0682802344651816, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65726525, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Improve performance of histogram `Record` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` when min and max are disabled using `NoMinMax`. (#7306)\\n\\n- Improve error handling for dropped data during translation by using `prometheus.NewInvalidMetric` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. ⚠️ **Breaking Change:** Previously, these cases were only logged and scrapes succeeded. Now, when translation would drop data (e.g., invalid label/value), the exporter emits a `NewInvalidMetric`, and Prometheus scrapes **fail with HTTP 500** by default. To preserve the prior behavior (scrapes succeed while errors are logged), configure your Prometheus HTTP handler with: `promhttp.HandlerOpts{ ErrorHandling: promhttp.ContinueOnError }`. (#7363)\\n\\n- Replace fnv hash with xxhash in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` for better performance. (#7371)\\n\\n- The default `TranslationStrategy` in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/prometheus` is changed from `otlptranslator.NoUTF8EscapingWithSuffixes` to `otlptranslator.UnderscoreEscapingWithSuffixes`. (#7421)\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n- Include W3C TraceFlags (bits 0–7) in the OTLP `Span.Flags` field in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp` and `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7438)\\n\\n- The `ErrorType` function in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0` now handles custom error types.\\n\\n  If an error implements an `ErrorType() string` method, the return value of that method will be used as the error type. (#7442)\\n\\n### Fixed\\n\\n- Fix `WithInstrumentationAttributes` options in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` to properly merge attributes when passed multiple times instead of replacing them. Attributes with duplicate keys will use the last value passed. (#7300)\\n\\n- The equality of `attribute.Set` when using the `Equal` method is not affected by the user overriding the empty set pointed to by `attribute.EmptySet` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute`. (#7357)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"improv perform of histogram record in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric when min and max are disabl use nominmax 7306 improv error handl for drop data dure translat by use prometheus newinvalidmetr in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus break chang previous these case were onli log and scrape succeed now when translat would drop data e g invalid label valu the export emit a newinvalidmetr and prometheus scrape fail with http 500 by default to preserv the prior behavior scrape succeed while error are log configur your prometheus http handler with promhttp handleropt errorhandl promhttp continueonerror 7363 replac fnv hash with xxhash in go opentelemetri io otel attribut for better perform 7371 the default translationstrategi in go opentelemetri io export prometheus is chang from otlptransl noutf8escapingwithsuffixes to otlptransl underscoreescapingwithsuffix 7421 improv perform of concurr measur in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7427 includ w3c traceflag bit 0 7 in the otlp span flag field in go opentelemetri io export otlp otlptrac otlptracehttp and go opentelemetri io export otlp otlptrac otlptracegrpc 7438 the errortyp function in go opentelemetri io otel semconv v1 37 0 now handl custom error type if an error implement an errortyp string method the return valu of that method will be use a the error type 7442 fix fix withinstrumentationattribut option in go opentelemetri io otel trace go opentelemetri io otel metric and go opentelemetri io otel log to proper merg attribut when pass multipl time instead of replac them attribut with duplic key will use the last valu pass 7300 the equal of attribut set when use the equal method is not affect by the user overrid the empti set point to by attribut emptyset in go opentelemetri io otel attribut 7357\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"2fc8f714ea7b265d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24004454963769917, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04552015662528452, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6939348, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Users Cannot Fix This Themselves\\n\\n This is middleware code that users cannot work around without forking the library. The race happens inside otelgin.Middleware(). A user who wants to use otelgin AND pass race detection has no choice but to:\\n\\n  1. Fork this library\\n\\n  2. Apply this exact fix\\n\\n  3. Maintain their fork indefinitely\\n\\n  This is not \\\"leaving the decision to users\\\"—it's forcing users to fork or live with failing race detection.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Precedent: This Project Has Fixed Similar Races Before\\n\\n  From the git history:\\n\\n  - #4577: \\\"otelgrpc: Fix data race in stats handlers\\\" (merged)\\n\\n  - #881: \\\"otelsarama: Fix WrapAsyncProducer race condition\\\" (merged)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston user can not fix this themselv this is middlewar code that user can not work around without fork the librari the race happen insid o