: 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:31:16Z\\n\\nI prefer using `require.NoError` because it ensures that no additional information distracts me when a test has already failed. I also searched the codebase and seems that both `require` and `assert` are used, and `require.NoError` appears more.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:35:44Z\\n\\nIt's hard to say, but in all cases, regardless of how many middlewares are chained, temporary files should be removed. I didn't check the return error of `RemoveAll` here, which aligns with the behavior in both Go's [`http` package](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e/src/net/http/server.go#L1727) and [echo-contrib](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90). I believe each middleware should independently attempt to remove temporary files.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T16:20:13Z\\n\\nsee: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609#issuecomment-2587572600\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go` — 2025-01-14T08:12:17Z\\n\\nRather than ignoring an error here, how about passing it to the otel error handler?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\terr := c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\totel.Handle(err)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-14T08:13:50Z\\n\\nI think what @flc1125 meant here is that you don't necessarily need to use `AbortWithError` (which also can return an error but ignores it), but instead call `require.NoError` here.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\trequire.NoError(err)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 31 16z i prefer use requir noerror becaus it ensur that no addit inform distract me when a test ha alreadi fail i also search the codebas and seem that both requir and assert are use and requir noerror appear more yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 35 44z it s hard to say but in all case regardless of how mani middlewar are chain temporari file should be remov i didn t check the return error of removeal here which align with the behavior in both go s http packag http github com golang go blob 44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e src net http server go l1727 and echo contrib http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 i believ each middlewar should independ attempt to remov temporari file flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t16 20 13z see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 issuecom 2587572600 dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go 2025 01 14t08 12 17z rather than ignor an error here how about pass it to the otel error handler suggest err c request multipartform removeal if err nil otel handl err dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 14t08 13 50z i think what flc1125 meant here is that you don t necessarili need to use abortwitherror which also can return an error but ignor it but instead call requir noerror here suggest requir noerror err\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"a6289f2135157364\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2720788229759757, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11331790710853673, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64252096, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"This PR fixes a concurrency bug in the OpenTelemetry Go SDK where the `AddAttributes`, `SetAttributes`, and `SetBody` methods on the `Record` type were mutating input parameters, causing race conditions when the same input data was used concurrently across multiple goroutines.\\n\\n- Implements defensive copying to prevent input mutation while maintaining performance optimizations\\n\\n- Adds comprehensive test coverage for various deduplication and truncation scenarios\\n\\n- Removes race condition workarounds that were previously skipping tests\\n\\n### Reviewed Changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 5 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated no comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n---\\n\\n<sub>**Tip:** Customize your code reviews with copilot-instructions.md. <a href=\\\"/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/new/main/.github?filename=copilot-instructions.md\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Create the file</a> or <a href=\\\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-rep